Prep: 15 mins - 20 mins
Cook: 15 mins
Serves 4
Can you reheat carbonara?
It is possible reheat carbonara, however fresh will give you the creamiest, silkiest texture. If you do wish to reheat, either add back to a frying pan with a splash of water and stir over a very low heat. Or tip into a heatproof bowl and set over a pan of just simmering water and keep stirring until hot.
What pasta is best for carbonara?
You can use almost any shape for carbonara, however it is long pasta that holds the sauce the best. Try bucatini, tagliatelle or linguine.
Can you use cream in carbonara?
An authentic carbonara does not use cream as the combination of the egg and cheese emulsified into a sauce provides the creamy, silky texture. However some prefer it with cream.
THE MAGIC INGREDIENT…
Pasta water can be dripped in as you transfer the spaghetti to the hot frying pan. Everything mingles to make a light, silky smooth sauce.
